# Family A3: consumer wait strategies (internal/wait). See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./internal/wait
BENCH=BenchmarkMemory/Wait
REF=chan
AUTO_KEY=wait
ADR=14
TITLE="Wait strategy (A3)"
# Full profile: IQMQ_BENCH_COLD_IDLE=1s for the spec's "wake after 1 s idle".

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="p99 under load with <= 1% idle CPU -> hybrid/eventcount; separate defaults for low/high contention allowed"
# MATRIX=default is the only grid: internal/wait's benchmark has no
# IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX branch, and its one grid is the row's own -- occupancy
# 0/50/95/100 with HDR quantiles, plus the idle-CPU burn and the wake latency
# after an idle period that §9.1 names beside them.
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="occupancy=0 occupancy=50 occupancy=95 occupancy=100 IdleCPU ColdWake"
DECIDED_ON="p99-ns p999-ns cpu-pct"
